\description{
An example \link[=om-class]{om} object representing two stocks managed jointly as a
single complex, each exploited by one fleet. The \code{Complexes} slot groups
both stocks so that data and management advice are aggregated across the
complex. Intended to illustrate stock complex construction.
Pairings of stocks, fleets, and observation models are for illustration
only and should not be taken as ecologically meaningful. See also
\link{SingleStockOM}, \link{TwoFleetOM}, and \link{MultiStockOM} for structural variants.
}
\details{
\subsection{Stocks}{

Two biologically contrasting stocks are included:
\itemize{
\item \link{AlbacoreExStock}: long-lived, slow-growing, low natural mortality.
\item \link{ButterfishExStock}: short-lived, fast-growing, high natural mortality.
}

See \link{AlbacoreExStock} and \link{ButterfishExStock} for full parameter details.
}

\subsection{Stock Complex}{

Setting \code{Complexes = list(StockComplex = 1:2)} instructs the operating
model to treat both stocks as a single management unit. Catch and index
data are aggregated across the complex when generating management advice,
while population dynamics are simulated independently for each stock.
}

\subsection{Fleet}{

\link{AsympExFleet} is applied to both stocks, representing a single fleet type
with asymptotic length-based selectivity. See \link{AsympExFleet} for full
parameter details.
}

\subsection{Observation Model}{

Because both stocks are aggregated into a single complex, the \code{Obs} slot
is indexed by complex and fleet rather than by individual stock. A single
\link{DataRichObs} object applies to the complex as a whole: landings, discards,
effort, a commercial CPUE index, a spawning-biomass survey, and annual
age- and length-composition samples from landed and discarded fish. A
fully-monitored scenario is appropriate here since joint management of a
stock complex relies on comprehensive, aggregated data across its member
stocks. See \link{DataRichObs} for full parameter details.
}

\subsection{Implementation Error}{

\link{FullComplianceImp} models perfect implementation: \code{TAC@Mean = 1}/
\code{SD = 0} and \code{Effort@Mean = 1}/\code{SD = 0} mean realised TAC/effort always
equal advice exactly, and
\code{Size@Compliance = 1} means any size-regulation advice (a change to
\code{Advice@Retention}/\code{Advice@Selectivity}) is adopted immediately by the
whole fleet (see \code{.UpdateSelectivitySim()}). See \code{\link[=Imp]{Imp()}} for details,
and \link{OverageImp}, \link{UnderageImp}, \link{PartialSizeComplianceImp} for
contrasting examples.
}
